# detail
Number of changes: 1

1. Modified | Function implementation
   Replaced the original index validation and conversion logic of `a2idx(j, n=None)` with importing and directly calling `sympy.matrices.common.a2idx`.
   The original implementation included:
   * Type checking and retrieval through `__index__()`;
   * Negative-index adjustment and range checking when `n` was not null;
   * Return of `int(j)`.

   The new implementation includes:
   * Import `a2idx` from `sympy.matrices.common` under the name `a2idx_`;
   * Directly `return a2idx_(j, n)`.
# /detail
